# Lantern: Ruined Beacon, polished

A restrained polish pass on the existing clean cut-paper belfry tableau. The same architecture, seven-color palette, suspended flame lantern, ravens, moon, thorns and stone path are retained. All artwork remains editable vector geometry: no raster art, textures, grain or gradients.

## Deliverables

All five silent H.264 / yuv420p MP4s are authored directly at **1920 × 1080, 60 fps**.

| File suffix | Duration | Frames | Purpose |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| Intro | 2 seconds | 120 | Theatre shutters open |
| Hold | 4 seconds | 240 | Seamless periodic loading loop |
| Complete | 2 seconds | 120 | Theatre shutters close |
| Preview | 8 seconds | 480 | Intro → Hold → Complete |
| Title | 9 seconds | 540 | Exact outlined title: Lantern |

Full prefix: `Lantern_D_RuinedBeacon_Polished_`.

`beacon_master.svg` is the editable loading master at hold time zero. `title_master.svg` is the settled title master. `render.py` contains the complete scene geometry, timing and native renderer; `title_glyphs.json` contains the seven outlined letterforms. There is no runtime font dependency. The inherited DejaVu Serif attribution is in `FONT_LICENSE.txt`.

## What changed

1. Ravens now face their actual horizontal travel, briefly turning edge-on as flat paper at the ends of their orbits. Far arcs pass behind the tower; near arcs cross below the lantern. Windblown leaves also pass behind the masonry, keeping the flame and cage unobstructed.
2. Wingbeats are calmer: five cycles per four-second hold instead of eight, with smaller articulated wing excursions and eased phase variation.
3. The hanging lantern is 78% of its prior size and swings ±3.2° instead of ±9°. The cage clears the alcove sides and the pendant has visible space above the sill. Its flame and counter-swing remain independently animated.
4. Background masonry is anchored instead of sliding sideways. Clouds, rope, foliage, leaves and birds provide environmental motion.
5. The title rises as intact outlined letterforms with much smaller rotations. All seven letters settle at 3.62 seconds; the ornament settles at 4.75 seconds. The fully settled title holds for 4.25 seconds through the end. Tracking increases slightly while the overall word remains centered.

## Playback contract

Play Intro once, Hold repeatedly, and Complete once. Start Complete at a Hold loop boundary. The conceptual endpoint of Intro equals Hold's start, Hold's four-second endpoint equals its start, and Complete starts at that same phase. Export sampling is half-open: the last stored frame is one frame before the conceptual endpoint, avoiding a duplicate held frame at a loop boundary.

Loading clips contain no visible text. The separate title does not fade away; it ends readable. The world continues moving behind the settled title. The 8-second Preview and 9-second Title are the native previews.

## Rebuild and verification

System requirements: Python 3, FFmpeg/FFprobe, Cairo, librsvg and GObject shared libraries. Debian/Ubuntu library package names include `libcairo2` and `librsvg2-2`. Python requirements are in `requirements.txt`.

Run `bash rebuild.sh` from an extracted copy. It regenerates all five native production MP4s, both SVG masters, poster proofs and validation outputs. The exporter uses a fixed two-thread libx264 encoder. Exact binary reproducibility is expected with the same renderer and codec versions; different Cairo, librsvg or FFmpeg versions may produce different bytes.

`verify.py` checks export metadata, frame counts, source phase equality, decoded motion, loop continuity, exact title lettering, settled-title stability and source/master correspondence. `check_clearance.py` raster-tests every one of the 240 native hold poses for raven overdraw intersecting the animated lantern silhouette, and confirms that the lantern silhouette stays inside the belfry aperture.

`manifest.json` lists SHA-256 hashes for every other file in this archive. Verify it before a rebuild, since a rebuild rewrites derived validation files. The archive excludes lower-resolution drafts, old clips and before/after review images.
